Enhancement: Show sizes when a cached pack file is too short

When a pack file in the cache was shorter than the data restic needed to
read, restic only reported that the cached file is too short. Restic now also
reports the size of the cached file and the number of bytes it needs. If the
pack is still too short after restic has fetched it from the repository again,
the error says so. This means the repository copy of the pack is shorter than
the index expects.

